#####Java 17 Interview Quick Revision — Before vs After####
#1. Records (Java 16, available in Java 17)
===========================================
Before — normal class

public class Customer {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public Customer(String name, int age) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }
}

After — Record

public record Customer(String name, int age) {}

Benefit: Automatically generates the constructor, accessors, equals(), hashCode() and toString().

Interview: Records are concise, shallowly immutable data-carrier classes, commonly useful for DTOs.

#2. Sealed Classes (Java 17)
==========================
Before — inheritance unrestricted

class Animal {}
class Dog extends Animal {}
class Cat extends Animal {}
class Tiger extends Animal {}

After — restrict inheritance

sealed class Animal permits Dog, Cat {}

final class Dog extends Animal {}
final class Cat extends Animal {}

Benefit: Only permitted classes can directly extend Animal.

Interview: Sealed classes provide controlled inheritance and make class hierarchies more predictable. 
